findings.description:
Step 4 handles "spawning, removal, profile changes queued during the tick". Nothing in the design can queue them:
- clients send nothing (line 43);
- the engine does not manage lifecycle (line 70);
- the environment interface is read-only (line 72).

Line 70's "removes entities when appropriate" is the only rule given. Predation kills, births, leaving world bounds and capacity exhaustion are all undefined. Line 84 sets a maximum entity count but not what happens to a spawn at the limit.

The document should name the producers of lifecycle events and where in the tick they are applied relative to ID assignment and logging.
